---
source: crates/omsh-syntax/tests/diagnostics.rs
expression: out
---
DoubleBracket
  what: the `[[ ... ]]` test
  help: use `[ ... ]` or `test`, and `case` for patterns
ProcessSubstitution
  what: process substitution
  help: write the output to a temporary file, or use a pipe
BraceExpansion
  what: brace expansion
  help: write the words out, or use a `for` loop; quote the braces to keep them as text
Array
  what: array syntax
  help: use separate variables, or the positional parameters with `set --`
Select
  what: the `select` loop
  help: use a `while` loop with `read`
Coprocess
  what: the `coproc` keyword
  help: use a pipe, or a named pipe made with `mkfifo`
Shopt
  what: the `shopt` command
  help: Oh My Shell has no shell options to switch; remove the command
PatternSubstitution
  what: the `${var/pattern/text}` replacement
  help: use `sed`, or `${var#prefix}` and `${var%suffix}`
Substring
  what: the `${var:offset:length}` substring form
  help: use `cut` or `expr substr`
CaseModification
  what: the `${var^}` and `${var,}` case change
  help: use `tr` to change the case of text
Indirection
  what: the `${!var}` indirect expansion
  help: use `eval` to read a variable named by another variable
Transformation
  what: the `${var@op}` transformation
  help: use the plain `${var}`
ArithmeticCommand
  what: the `(( ... ))` arithmetic command
  help: use `: $((...))` to run an expression, or `[ $((...)) -ne 0 ]` to test it
FunctionKeyword
  what: the `function` keyword
  help: write `name() { ...; }` instead
PipeStderr
  what: the `|&` pipe
  help: write `2>&1 |` instead
CaseFallthrough
  what: the `;&` and `;;&` ending of a `case` branch
  help: end each branch with `;;`
AppendAssignment
  what: the `name+=value` assignment
  help: write `name="${name}value"` instead
FileContents
  what: the `$(<file)` shortcut
  help: use `$(cat file)` instead
